terized in musical genres ranging from instrumental pieces and popular songs to oratorios, ballets, and operas. Locke's study offers new insights into much-loved masterworks by composers such as Cavalli, Lully, Purcell, Rameau, Handel, Vivaldi, Gluck, and Mozart. In these works, evocations of ethnic and cultural Otherness often mingle attraction with envy or fear, and some pieces were understood at the time as commenting on conditions in Europe itself.","publicationYear":2015,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Music, history and criticism, 16th century","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-music-and-the-exotic-from-the-renaissance-to-mozart-ralph-p-locke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Music, history and criticism, 17th century","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-music-and-the-exotic-from-the-renaissance-to-mozart-ralph-p-locke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Music, history and criticism, 18th century","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-music-and-the-exotic-from-the-renaissance-to-mozart-ralph-p-locke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Music","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-music-and-the-exotic-from-the-renaissance-to-mozart-ralph-p-locke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History and criticism","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-music-and-the-exotic-from-the-renaissance-to-mozart-ralph-p-locke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Exoticism in music","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-music-and-the-exotic-from-the-renaissance-to-mozart-ralph-p-locke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Exoticism in opera","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-music-and-the-exotic-from-the-renaissance-to-mozart-ralph-p-locke"}],"displaySummary":"In this prequel to his 2009 book Musical Exoticism, Ralph P